CVE-2026-41225 affects BIG-IP, not BIG-IQ, and is fixed in versions 21.0.0.2, 17.5.1.6 and 17.1.3.2, with the 16.1 branch past end of technical support; F5 published the quarterly notification on 2026-05-13. The flaw needs an authenticated Manager-role account with network access to iControl REST and has no data-plane exposure; no source describes a credential-theft chain or a European public-sector deployment base, and the list of secondary CVE ids by flaw class did not match NCSC-NL's advisory. F5 scores it CVSS 4.0 8.6, and NCSC-NL's 9.1 is a CVSS 3.1 score with a changed scope.
